
1. Requirement Gathering	            5 min
2. Core Entities & Relationships     	7 min
3. Class Design                      	8 min
4. Workflows & Design Patterns      	7 min
5. UML Diagram	                      5 min
6. Edge Cases & Design              	5 min
7. Implementation & Coding          	8 min

Total	45 min	

1. Requirement Gathering:

Functional requirements,
non-functional requirements,
scope,
assumptions,
and clarifying questions.

2. Core Entities & Relationships:

Entities,
attributes,
associations,
cardinality,
inheritance,
composition,
and aggregation.

3. Class Design: 

Classes,
objects, 
constructors,
methods, 
interfaces,
abstract classes, 
encapsulation,
and SOLID principles.

4. Workflows & Design Patterns:

Use cases, sequence of operations,
Strategy,
Factory,
Observer,
and State patterns.

5. UML Diagram: 

Class diagrams,
sequence diagrams,
association,
inheritance,
composition,
aggregation,
and multiplicity.

6. Edge Cases & Design:

Validation,
exceptions, 
concurrency,
race conditions, 
extensibility,
and separation of concerns.



7. Implementation & Coding:

Folder structure,
interfaces,
concrete classes,
service classes, 
repositories,
enums, 
and executable workflows.














